rooms={

 'poolgarden':{'title':'Pool garden · Proposed only','headline':'A calm place to swim, sit and unwind.','intro':'Pale timber loungers, ivory cushions and useful pavilion seating bring the house palette into the garden.','variants':['compact'],'fullRoom':'proposal-pool-terrace','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Keep a dry route beside the water.','Three 2.05 m loungers turn along the west deck, leaving a continuous paved route on the pool side. Slats, adjustable backs, hinge fixings, wheels, cushion seams and folded towels are modelled. The pool, coping, hot tub and existing terrace outline remain.'),
  ('Give the loggia a purpose.','A compact sofa, stone coffee table and shallow sliding towel cupboard create a sheltered sitting area. The route to the summer house, changing corner, tool store and garden WC stays clear. The summer-house step now meets the actual raised floor with two equal rises.'),
  ('Keep the proposal differences.','This pool and loggia are part of Proposed. The Planning variant retains its current garden layout. These are model-based furnishing and circulation studies; the pool construction and final outdoor materials remain part of detailed design.') ]},
 'gardenhouse':{'title':'Summer house, changing & garden WC','headline':'Small garden rooms, properly thought through.','intro':'A two-seat bench, private changing corner and useful fittings work within the retained narrow garden-building shells.','fullRoom':'2445694-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Make the narrow summer house useful.','An upholstered oak bench sits at one end, with a shallow drinks cupboard and a separate changing bench at the other. A gathered ivory curtain provides privacy. Hooks, towel borders, hollow cups, cabinet pulls and individual tool fittings are modelled.'),
  ('Fit the actual rooms.','The compact WC has a 640 mm basin, wall-hung pan, mirror, bronze mixer and serviceable storage. The small tool store uses a shallow far-wall rack. Existing door apertures stay in place; the complete new leaves are checked through their swings.'),
  ('Connect to each garden.','Proposed opens onto the loggia with intermediate steps to the raised floors. Planning retains the glazed summer-house frontage, with one bay becoming an outward-opening door. Bounded proposal-only corrections clear existing kerb and hedge geometry from the retained shells and WC doorway. The original reconstruction remains unchanged.') ]},
 'office':{'title':'Original ground-floor office','headline':'A light workspace with room to pause.','intro':'A pale oak desk faces into the room, with daylight from the bay, closed storage and a separate reading chair.','fullRoom':'2445661-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Work with the daylight.','The 1.80 × 0.80 m desk places the screen perpendicular to the main bay glazing. The adjustable chair, keyboard keys, monitor controls, cable tray, grommet and pencil drawer are modelled. Ivory linen blinds replace the former coloured curtains.'),
  ('Anchor the furniture.','The reading chair backs towards the east wall, while sliding cupboards and books use the north wall. The centre and hall approach remain open. The plant sits clear of the walls, radiator and desk approach.'),
  ('Retain the room you have.','The bay, structural walls, radiator and original double hall doors remain. The study checks furniture fit, door movements, knee space and occupied routes. The final workstation can be adjusted to its user.') ]},
 'workshop':{'title':'Garden workshop · Proposed only','headline':'A clear, daylit place to make.','intro':'A long oak workbench, mobile assembly table and closed tool storage make the retained workshop useful and calm.','variants':['compact'],'fullRoom':'proposal-garden-workshop','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Put daylight over the work.','The 5.4 m bench sits below the north windows, 900 mm above the actual floor. Hollow drawers, runners, vice jaws, screw threads, tool grips, socket apertures and carry-case latches are modelled. Linear lights attach below the measured ceiling.'),
  ('Keep the centre flexible.','A 1.6 × 0.8 m mobile table has locking castors and a lower shelf. Sliding storage uses the west wall, leaving a clear entry and central aisle. The complete door and drawers are reviewed alongside working positions.'),
  ('Preserve the garden layout.','The Proposed-only workshop footprint, windows, roof and existing 880 mm strip path remain. Light interior faces and bounded proposal-only hedge clearance resolve the existing visual intrusions. Final tools and services should follow the hobby you choose; no large fixed machinery is assumed.') ]},
 'garage':{'title':'Double garage & parking','headline':'Two cars, useful storage, clear everyday routes.','intro':'A restrained warm-grey garage with oak and stone fittings, keeping the existing doors and adding a fourth outdoor space on the drive.','fullRoom':'proposal-new-double-garage','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Park first, fit storage around it.','The two existing 4.4 × 1.8 m concept cars are staggered, leaving room for an east-wall worktop and closed storage beside the southern car. Complete drawers, tool handles, socket apertures, chargers, coiled cables and restrained ceiling fittings are modelled. The garage opening, window and both house connections remain.'),
  ('Check how the room works.','Walking routes use a 600 mm body and 42-degree front-door envelopes. The house, utility, chargers and storage remain connected with either car’s front doors open, or both drivers’ doors open. With all four front doors open together, a door must close to pass between the separated areas. This retained garage does not offer unrestricted door opening; the actual household vehicles need checking.'),
  ('Keep four outdoor spaces.','A fourth 4.8 × 2.5 m compact-car space occupies the existing resin drive, preserving the front lawn and pedestrian court. Arrival and departure are checked with the other bays occupied, including the two garage cars, and the pedestrian route to the entrance stays connected. Vehicle dimensions and surveyed site geometry remain the basis for final tracking.') ]},
 'landings':{'title':'Upper landings & library','headline':'Useful storage, room to move.','intro':'Warm oak, concealed linen storage and a quiet reading corner connect the bedrooms without filling their routes.','fullRoom':'proposal-landing-library','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Let circulation lead.','The reading chair and stone table sit beneath the loft stair, with a cordless bronze table lamp and a clear approach in front. A shallow bookcase uses the upper gallery wall beside the principal-suite approach. The path along the entrance void and the approach to the loft stair stay open, including with the chair occupied.'),
  ('Put storage in the wider space.','The connecting landing receives 2.10 m of linen storage with sliding fronts and a coordinated wall of books, objects and closed cupboards. The retained bedroom openings stay clear. Individual books, folded linen, cupboard tracks, pulls and chair upholstery details are modelled.'),
  ('Keep the retained architecture.','Oak flooring and quiet relief art connect the first-floor route. The stair openings, voids, radiator, glazing and structural walls remain; the original stair receives coordinated oak and bronze finishes. The isolated study checks furniture fit, floor support, door movements, sliding panels and occupied routes. The separate low-headroom loft bridge remains flagged in its own study.') ]},
 'arrival':{'title':'Entrance & ground-floor halls','headline':'A calm arrival, a clear route onward.','intro':'Useful coat and shoe storage, a softly lit double-height entrance and simpler fittings in the original hall.','fullRoom':'proposal-new-entrance-gallery','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Give everyday things a place.','Two 320 mm-deep oak and ivory joinery legs wrap the wall corner. End-on hanging keeps coats within the shallow cabinet; the return has a bag bay, drawer and stone key shelf with charging. A separate 1.43 m shoe bench sits below the retained gym window. Occupied coat and bench positions leave the onward route clear.'),
  ('Keep the architecture open.','The front doors, entrance link, glass-lined garden passage, basement stair opening and upper guards stay in place. Three restrained opal pendants hang from the measured sloping roof, above the walking route. Limestone flooring and a single plant connect the entrance with the original hall. The cutaway removes the upper storeys to reveal this ground-floor sequence.'),
  ('Simplify the old hall.','The original steps keep their geometry, with oak treads, ivory risers and simple bronze balusters beneath oak handrails. The radiator and door openings remain. Plain stone niche shelves, small ceramics and bronze/opal lights replace the ornate fittings without recutting the wall apertures. A narrow full-height mirror and shallow relief artwork complete the hall. Complete door sweeps, drawer travel, furniture fit and occupied routes are checked; final joinery, electrics and site dimensions need detailed design.') ]},
 'terrace':{'title':'Roof terrace · Proposed only','headline':'An outdoor room with space around it.','intro':'Pale timber, ivory cushions and honed stone form a relaxed sitting group and a separate four-seat café table. This terrace exists in Proposed only; Planning retains its roof and family-lounge window.','variants':['compact'],'fullRoom':'proposal-shared-roof-terrace','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Make two comfortable places.','A two-seat sofa faces two individual lounge chairs, with a small oval stone table between them. The round café table provides four regular places. Slatted timber frames, shaped back rails, cushion seams, fixings, lamps and tableware are modelled in the same restrained palette as the house.'),
  ('Keep the rooflights and routes clear.','The existing terrace doors, three flush rooflights, stone surface, guards, west privacy screen and drainage remain. Furniture is set back from the outer guards and stays off the rooflights. Checked routes reach every seating group and the perimeter without crossing glass. Low cushion storage and two modest planters sit near the building.'),
  ('Preserve the differences between the proposals.','This study is available for Proposed only. It does not add a terrace to Planning. The furniture layout is checked in ordinary and occupied use; roof construction, loading, wind restraint, waterproofing, guard and rooflight details still need project-specific design. Cushions should be stored indoors in bad weather.') ]},
 'hobby':{'title':'Loft hobby room & bridge','headline':'Space to make, read and change things.','intro':'A movable oak worktable, useful low storage and a relaxed sitting group leave the centre open for different hobbies.','fullRoom':'proposal-loft-studio-and-lounge','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Give making a proper place.','The 2.00 × 1.05 m project table has two regular chairs, lockable castors and a clear approach. Supplies sit in sliding cupboards below the dormer windows. Low archive storage follows the opposite roof slope, with books gathered near the sitting area.'),
  ('Keep the middle flexible.','An ivory sofa and curved reading chair face a small limestone table at the east end. The middle stays clear for a changing project. Oak floors, linen blinds, small plants and restrained bronze details continue through the room, bridge and landing. The windows, roof, stairs and guards remain.'),
  ('Recognise the low areas.','The eaves doors retain their low openings and lead to stooping storage. The retained bridge beside the loft stair is also constrained: along the usable route, measured clearance is approximately 1.78–1.90 m. The room furnishings and doors fit, but this bridge is not a full-height route for taller people. Its headroom needs resolving in detailed design before construction; this study retains the existing roof and stair geometry for review.') ]},
 'loftsuite':{'title':'Loft bedroom & ensuite','headline':'Let the roof shape the room.','intro':'A wall-backed king bed, fitted oak storage and a limestone ensuite arranged within the existing dormer.','fullRoom':'proposal-new-loft-studio','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Keep the standing routes in the taller space.','The 1.50 × 2.00 m king bed sits against the bathroom partition. Both sides and the foot have checked routes beneath the measured roof. A compact 205 mm bedside perch beside the ensuite preserves its doorway; the opposite bedside is larger. The solid bedroom entrance wall stays in place.'),
  ('Use the lower space for storage.','A 1.97 m sliding wardrobe occupies the entrance wall, with hanging rails, shelves and folded-linen storage. The low eaves cupboards and hip-store shelving have been removed at owner review, leaving these floor areas clear. The hip store retains its low doorway and sloping roof. Oak, ivory, wool and a restrained green plant continue the house palette.'),
  ('Fit the bathroom to the dormer.','The roof, windows, partitions and door apertures remain. The basin and WC keep broadly familiar service positions. A low shower tray and lower rainfall fitting suit the approximately 2.09 m ceiling. The shower leaf opens inward and the hip-store door opens into the bathroom to avoid the roof. Complete door sweeps, roof fit and separate circulation states are checked in the native models. Final waterproofing, fittings, service routes and site dimensions need detailed design.') ]},
 'sidebed':{'title':'Side-wing bedroom & ensuite','headline':'Make a compact suite feel settled.','intro':'A wall-backed double, useful fitted storage and a limestone ensuite, with a clearer route between them.','fullRoom':'proposal-side-wing-south-bedroom','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Put the bed on a solid wall.','The 1.35 × 1.90 m double turns against the solid east wall, with a slim upholstered frame, oak backdrop and two floating bedsides. There is 940 mm beside the south bed edge and 835 mm beside the north edge, plus a 665 mm route at the foot. A shallow luggage bench sits beneath the west window.'),
  ('Release the corner by the door.','The bedroom entrance partition moves north into the family approach; its main seating arrangement stays intact. The ensuite east partition moves 350 mm west of the original layout. The bedroom door keeps its 850 mm opening. A 1.11 m sliding wardrobe provides 590 mm-deep storage and ends clear of the west window.'),
  ('Keep the bathroom practical.','The one-metre shower and WC keep their service positions. A shallower 360 mm basin unit moves with the partition and has sliding oak fronts, an open bowl, lit mirror and bronze fittings. All three complete doors and the rebuilt junctions are checked, along with seven separate use states using a 600 mm body. This remains a compact single-user ensuite, with final services, enclosure hardware and site dimensions to be detailed.') ]},
 'formal':{'title':'Formal lounge & dining','headline':'A room for conversation and gathering.','intro':'Facing ivory sofas, the original fireplace and an eight-seat round oak table centred in the dining bay.','fullRoom':'2445666-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('A settled conversation group.','Two generous three-seat sofas face across a slim limestone table, with the existing fireplace at one end. Oak boards, a wool rug, linen and restrained bronze fittings connect the room to the accepted interiors. A curved reading chair and small stone table give the front bay a separate use. The radiator, kitchen hatch and garden openings remain.'),
  ('Eight places around one table.','The owner-approved 1.70 m round oak pedestal table is centred in the hexagonal dining area, with eight upholstered chairs and a re-centred pendant. The existing lounge and drinks cabinet are retained.'),
  ('Detail the room around movement.','New oak hall leaves use room-side hinges in the existing openings, with different opening stops to suit each return. The chair footprints and 400 mm pullback fit the dining bay. Passing and serving beside the west drinks cabinet remain tight when chairs are occupied; furniture fit is not a claim of unrestricted circulation. Final table, chairs and site dimensions remain to be confirmed.') ]},
 'bedroom4':{'title':'Bedroom 4 & ensuite','headline':'Make a smaller room work well.','intro':'A wall-backed double, useful fitted storage and a carefully rearranged compact ensuite.','fullRoom':'2445676-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Keep a proper bed and a clear arrival.','The 1.35 × 1.90 m double sits against the solid north wall in a complete upholstered frame. Shallow floating bedsides, individual reading lights and charging controls sit on an oak backdrop. A 2 m sliding wardrobe provides proper 650 mm-deep hanging and shelf space. The front window and radiator remain.'),
  ('Give the ensuite a more useful shower.','An 800 × 900 mm shower replaces the previous approximately 680 × 710 mm tray. This requires moving the short return 113 mm west and rebuilding its connection to the linen-cupboard back wall. Both door apertures remain; the ensuite leaf opens into the bedroom. A 900 mm floating vanity and compact concealed-cistern WC keep the main service positions.'),
  ('Be honest about a compact pair of rooms.','A king bed blocked the route with the bathroom door open, so the new bed retains the original double size. The full frame leaves about 819 mm to the radiator, with a 640 mm single-file west aisle. Seven use states are checked with a 600 mm body, alongside complete door sweeps, drawer travel and the wall junction. The ensuite is for one person at a time. Selected fittings, enclosure stop, services and measured site dimensions still require detailed design.') ]},
 'familybath':{'title':'Family bathroom','headline':'A calmer room for everyday bathing.','intro':'A full fitted bath, floating oak vanity and restrained limestone and bronze details.','fullRoom':'2445671-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Keep the useful service layout.','The bath stays beneath the north privacy window, with the basin on the west wall and WC on the east. A 1.20 m floating oak vanity replaces the previous 1.73 m cabinet run. Its recessed basin, service-cutout drawer, lit mirror and small fittings give the room a cleaner centre.'),
  ('Finish the bath properly.','The 1.88 × 0.78 m fitted bath has a modelled bathing well, rim, waste, overflow and serviceable limestone apron. Bronze controls and a flexible hand shower sit at the front of the east wall. The existing privacy glass and white window board remain. Towels sit close to the bath, outside the basin approach.'),
  ('Check the room in use.','The retained 832 mm hall opening receives a new right-hinged inward oak leaf, avoiding the pinch at the WC approach. Six separate use states cover arrival, closed door, basin use, WC use, drying and the extended drawer with a 600 mm body. Door, drawer and bathing-well geometry are checked in the native model. Final fittings, waterproofing, services and measured clearances still need detailed selection.') ]},
 'bedroom3':{'title':'Bedroom 3','headline':'A settled bed, a clear outlook.','intro':'A slim upholstered king bed, fitted oak storage and a useful place to sit on arrival.','fullRoom':'2445679-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Keep the useful bed wall.','The king bed stays against the solid south wall, with a complete slim frame, upholstered headboard and floating stone-topped bedsides. Individual reading lights, switches and charging points sit on an oak backdrop. Warm wool carpet and ivory bedding carry the house palette into the room.'),
  ('Make storage fit properly.','A 2.10 m sliding wardrobe replaces the previous 1.70 m run. Its 650 mm depth sits inside the retained skirting. A recessed Roman blind keeps the window and radiator clear of loose fabric. The hall opening and original outward-opening balcony door remain.'),
  ('Leave room for everyday movement.','The luggage perch sits beyond the entrance turn, so someone seated there does not block arrival. A new inward oak hall leaf fits the existing 778 mm opening. The full bed frame leaves approximately 679 mm to the radiator; this and the wardrobe approach are single-file routes. Six use states are checked with a 600 mm body, and both complete door assemblies are tested through their sweeps. Final products and site dimensions still need verification.') ]},
 'bedroom2':{'title':'Bedroom 2','headline':'A calm room with space to breathe.','intro':'A warm oak bed wall, more useful fitted storage and a quiet reading corner.','fullRoom':'2445672-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Keep a good bed position.','The king bed stays against the solid east wall, with a complete upholstered frame, floating oak bedsides, individual reading lights and charging controls. Soft ivory bedding, a woven throw and warm wool carpet carry through the agreed house palette.'),
  ('Give storage a better place.','A 2.0 m wardrobe replaces the 1.55 m north-wall run. Its 650 mm depth accommodates proper hanging space and shelves; sliding fronts keep the approach clear. A curved reading chair and small limestone table sit in the north corner. The front window and radiator stay accessible beneath a recessed Roman blind.'),
  ('Make arrival work in use.','The existing 737 mm doorway stays in place. A new oak leaf opens inward, clear of the wardrobe, instead of projecting into the hall. Six 600 mm-body checks cover the ordinary room, closed door, wardrobe use, occupied reader and each occupied bedside. The reading corner and bed-side passages are for one person at a time. Final hardware and site dimensions still need verification.') ]},
 'cloakroom':{'title':'Cloakroom','headline':'A clearer, calmer small room.','intro':'A floating oak vanity, limestone surfaces and carefully fitted bronze details.','fullRoom':'2445660-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Keep the shell, simplify the fittings.','A 900 mm floating vanity replaces the previous 1.68 m cabinet run. Its recessed basin, wall mixer and lit mirror leave a clearer arrival. The WC stays on the south service wall, with a concealed cistern and a simple relief artwork above.'),
  ('Remove what is no longer useful.','The former south window is already bricked up in both proposals. Its old curtains are removed and the inner wall is finished in ivory. The existing hall doorway stays in place. Oak, limestone and bronze connect this small room to the rest of the house.'),
  ('A compact room for one person.','The retained doorway is approximately 679 mm wide. A 600 mm body has been checked with the door open, closed and the upper vanity drawer extended. The U-shaped drawer clears the basin and waste assembly. Storage is reduced, and basin and WC use share the floor area. Final ventilation, plumbing and purchased fittings still need detailed selection.') ]},
 'family':{'title':'Upstairs family lounge','headline':'A quieter place to share.','intro':'A comfortable sofa, books and games, with a small writing desk and garden outlook.','fullRoom':'proposal-upstairs-family-lounge','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('A settled sitting area.','The three-seat ivory sofa sits fully against the solid south wall, with individual reading lights and a simple relief artwork. Low limestone tables, warm oak and a soft wool rug continue the house palette. Books, games and a small plant sit in shallow fitted storage.'),
  ('A useful place to write.','The north-facing desk receives light from the west window at the side. Its rounded oak top, upholstered chair, task lamp and charging points suit occasional writing or homework. At 1.14 m wide it is smaller than the previous 1.6 m desk, with a deeper 600 mm surface.'),
  ('Keep the routes clear.','The table shape and positions leave access around the sitting group, including with the chair pulled back or the sofa occupied. Proposed retains its terrace doors with fitted handles; Planning retains its north window and has no terrace. The narrow space at the storage front is for one person at a time. The existing room shell, landing connection and bedroom doorway stay in place.') ]},
 'guest':{'title':'Garden guest bedroom','headline':'A restful room with a garden outlook.','intro':'A wall-backed super-king bed, useful fitted storage and a quiet place to read.','fullRoom':'2445673-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('A settled place for the bed.','The bed sits against the solid east wall, with an upholstered headboard, floating oak bedsides and individual reading lights. A fixed 43-inch television fits the short wall between the doorways. Full-height ivory curtains, warm wool carpet and a curved reading chair soften the retained room.'),
  ('Storage without blocking the view.','A 3.675 m fitted wardrobe runs along the south wall, using sliding fronts to keep the aisle free. It replaces the previous 4.24 m run. The window and radiator stay clear, and the reading table sits back from the route around the bed.'),
  ('The measured trade-offs.','The wardrobe-to-bed aisle is 855 mm. Someone choosing clothes occupies that side while the other bedside, ensuite and balcony remain reachable. The fixed television has a modest image size at this distance. The ensuite door opens into the bedroom to release space in the compact bathroom; the existing doorway stays in place.') ]},
 'guestbath':{'title':'Guest ensuite','headline':'A compact bathroom, carefully fitted.','intro':'A floating oak basin unit, limestone shower and restrained bronze fittings.','fullRoom':'2445675-0','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Keep the useful arrangement.','The shower stays in the south recess, the WC below the north window and the basin along the west service wall. A 900 mm floating oak unit, recessed ceramic basin and lit mirror create a cleaner room. The existing window remains; a simple linen blind replaces the heavy curtains.'),
  ('Make the door movements work.','The bedroom door opens outward. The shower door opens inward to an 85-degree stop, with its double-sided handle clear of the wall and room to stand inside while closing it. The shower controls are on the back wall, away from the moving glass.'),
  ('A small, single-user room.','The shower entry is approximately 612 mm wide and remains tight. The basin and WC share standing space. The layout checks these uses separately and tests a 600 mm body through the shower. This is a developed concept: the actual enclosure, opening stop, waterproofing and services need selection against measured site dimensions.') ]},
 'utility':{'title':'Utility','headline':'A calm, practical laundry.','intro':'One fitted oak run, a generous clear aisle and a useful place to fold.','fullRoom':'proposal-utility','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('Everything in a useful sequence.','The washer and dryer face into the room beneath a shared folding surface. A pull-out laundry hamper, undermount sink and tall storage complete the run. Oak, limestone, ivory appliance fronts and bronze details continue the house palette. The existing window brings light above the worktop.'),
  ('Small changes, better movement.','The room retains its walls, window and both door openings. The garage door is rehung on the other jamb so its open leaf stays away from the working area. The sink remains on the east service wall with a local position adjustment. There is no WC.'),
  ('Checked in use.','The aisle measures 1.595 m to the worktop. Open appliance doors, the pulled-out hamper, folding and sink use have each been checked with a 600 mm navigation body and the room doors open. These are separate working states. Final appliance dimensions, service connections and the garage door specification still need detailed selection.') ]},
 'gym':{'title':'Gym','headline':'Space to train, room to move.','intro':'Two gate-facing treadmills, a clear entrance and useful oak storage.','fullRoom':'proposal-gym','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('A calmer training room.','Warm grey rubber, natural oak and ivory carry the house palette into the gym. A full-size dumbbell bench, eight pairs of weights and a west-facing bike have their own places. The extra cable tower is omitted to keep the utility route open. Towels, water and a rolled mat are gathered beside the utility. The windows remain clear and the room has no mirror.'),
  ('Two exercise modes.','Both treadmills have a clear two-metre run-off behind them. The rower is stored in two parts in the default model. For rowing, both treadmills are switched off and the marked rear floor area is used instead. The bench stays in place. The measured plan shows these distinct arrangements.'),
  ('The practical limits.','The hall door moves 300 mm south, with the neighbouring internal window 200 mm south. The courtyard route passes east of the rear safety zones. Running, rowing, cycling and bench exercises have been checked as separate activities; this is not a claim that every station can operate together. The previous barbell rack and loose ball have been removed to improve access. Final equipment, selected exercises, fixings, floor loads and ventilation require detailed review.') ]},
 'cinema':{'title':'Cinema','headline':'A quieter place to watch.','intro':'Deep seats, warm fabric and oak, with a clear view from every place.','fullRoom':'proposal-basement-cinema','plan':'arrangements.svg','copy':[
  ('One comfortable row.','Four generous fixed seats face a 2.6 m screen. A low limestone table leaves a 650 mm approach to the seats; the wider eastern aisle leads back to the door. Cup holders and charging are built into the centre console, with shallow storage for blankets behind the sofa.'),
  ('An explicit trade-off.','This arrangement has four places, compared with six in the previous two-row layout. It removes the rear platform and keeps other viewers out of the screen sightline. The seat approach is single-file and passing in front of occupied knees still requires people to tuck in. The fabric, oak divisions and low lighting soften the room; sound isolation, ventilation and final equipment remain to be designed.') ]},
 'bar':{'title':'Wine bar & games','headline':'Room to serve, sit and play.','intro':'A fitted oak and limestone bar, a comfortable TV group and separate spaces for pool and darts.','fullRoom':'proposal-basement-bar','plan':'layout-plan.svg','copy':[
  ('A usable serving space.','The two-metre bar keeps three places, with upholstered stools, a bronze footrail and a proper knee overhang. Behind it, a 1.3 m clear working aisle gives access to the wine cooler, drinks cooler, drawers and glass storage. This is a dry bar; glass washing stays in the utility or kitchen.'),
  ('Each activity has its own place.','A standard 6-foot British pool table turns across the room, with full-length cue space around the playing surface. The darts zone sits separately between the pool and bar, away from the cinema route. The west-facing sofa has its own fixed TV and controller table.'),
  ('The space that remains tight.','With the full pool-playing area reserved, the passing strip beside the stairs is about 620 mm wide. It works as single-file access, not a broad principal route. The measured plan shows this alongside occupied stools and the separate darts area. Equipment selection, delivery, acoustics and ventilation still need detailed review.') ]}
}
